<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Eritrea (federation)</h1><p class="st-meta">1952 CE – 1962 CE · capital Asmara</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Eritrea's decade as an autonomous unit federated with Ethiopia, whose dismantling by Haile Selassie set off a 30-year war for independence.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Following a UN resolution of December 1950, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-eritrea">Eritrea</a> was federated with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/federal-democratic-republic-of-ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> under the Ethiopian Crown in September 1952. It received its own constitution, an elected assembly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asmara">Asmara</a>, an executive and official languages, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigrinya-language">Tigrinya</a> and Arabic, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> controlled defence, foreign affairs, currency and trade.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The federation was unequal from the start. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haile-selassie">Haile Selassie's</a> representative steadily curtailed Eritrean autonomy: political parties and independent newspapers were suppressed, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amharic">Amharic</a> was imposed, and the Eritrean flag was replaced by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia's</a> in 1958. Nationalists organised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrean-liberation-movement">Eritrean Liberation Movement</a> in 1958 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrean-liberation-front">Eritrean Liberation Front</a> in 1960, whose fighters under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamid-idris-awate">Hamid Idris Awate</a> began armed struggle in September 1961.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In November 1962 the Eritrean assembly, under pressure, voted to dissolve itself, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-eritrea">Eritrea</a> was annexed as a province of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a>. The war that followed ended with independence as the State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrea">Eritrea</a> in 1993.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/eritrea-federation.jpg" alt="Eritrea (federation)" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Orange Tuesday Original uploader was Orange Tuesday at en.wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Eritrea_(1952-1961).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1952 CE – 1962 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Asmara</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Tedla Bairu</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ethiopian Orthodox Christianity, Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Tigrinya, Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/eritrea">Eritrea</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Federal Eritrea, Autonomous Eritrea</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1957&amp;focus=eritrea-federation" aria-label="Eritrea (federation) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5750 1840 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Eritrea (federation) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6070 2096L6063 1863M6070 2096L6029 1964"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6063 1863h0M6029 1964h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6070 2096h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6070 2096h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1957&amp;focus=eritrea-federation">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
